  "question": "Does our account-lockout setup satisfy Part 5.7?",
  "answer": "I cannot determine if your setup satisfies the requirement because I do not have access to your operator-side documentation (such as your system configurations, security policies, or account-lockout parameters) in this conversation.\n\nHowever, I can define the specific duty you must meet. Under **CIP-007-6 R5 Part 5.7**, for High Impact BES Cyber Systems (and their associated EACMS, PACS, and PCA) and Medium Impact BES Cyber Systems at Control Centers (and their associated EACMS, PACS, and PCA), you must meet the following requirement **where technically feasible**:\n\nYou must implement **one** of the following two actions:\n1.  **Limit the number of unsuccessful authentication attempts** (account lockout); **OR**\n2.  **Generate alerts** after a specific threshold of unsuccessful authentication attempts is reached.\n\n**Compliance Note:**\nThe standard provides a choice between two permitted actions. To confirm compliance, you should verify that your current configuration either enforces a lockout or triggers an alert, and that you have documentation (such as account-lockout parameters or alerting rules) available as evidence [csection-98ce4ada99c0ad8c57dd].\n\nIf you can provide your internal configuration details or security policy text, I can perform the comparison for you.\n\nCited sections:\n- csection-98ce4ada99c0ad8c57dd (CIP-007-6 R5 Part 5.7 requirement text)",
